1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,800
GitHub just added a way to

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:03,733
test your Copilot skills and

3
00:00:03,733 --> 00:00:04,800
MCP tools.

4
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,833
AI output can change from one

5
00:00:06,833 --> 00:00:08,333
run to the next.

6
00:00:08,333 --> 00:00:10,333
So one good answer does not

7
00:00:10,333 --> 00:00:11,567
prove your skill,

8
00:00:11,567 --> 00:00:13,667
agent or MCP tool works.

9
00:00:13,667 --> 00:00:15,500
That is why evals exist.

10
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:17,667
An eval is a repeatable test

11
00:00:17,667 --> 00:00:19,233
for AI behavior.

12
00:00:19,233 --> 00:00:21,033
You give an agent a realistic

13
00:00:21,033 --> 00:00:22,633
task, describe what a good

14
00:00:22,633 --> 00:00:24,100
result looks like,

15
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:25,733
and check the result and how

16
00:00:25,733 --> 00:00:27,267
the agent got there.

17
00:00:27,267 --> 00:00:28,567
In Copilot Evals,

18
00:00:28,567 --> 00:00:30,600
you ask Copilot in your own

19
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:32,733
words, or use the slash eval

20
00:00:32,733 --> 00:00:33,667
command.

21
00:00:33,667 --> 00:00:35,000
You approve each run,

22
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,767
then see which checks passed

23
00:00:36,767 --> 00:00:37,833
and failed.

24
00:00:37,833 --> 00:00:39,067
Change your skill,

25
00:00:39,067 --> 00:00:40,467
rerun the same eval,

26
00:00:40,467 --> 00:00:42,800
and compare before and after.

27
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,533
It is in public preview,

28
00:00:44,533 --> 00:00:45,633
for Individual,

29
00:00:45,633 --> 00:00:47,800
Business and Enterprise plans.

30
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:50,067
What would you test first?

